# Required for the sync Netlify Function.
# Set in Netlify: Site configuration → Environment variables
#
# GITHUB_TOKEN (required):
# - Classic PAT: needs "repo" scope (full control of repositories)
# - If pushing to org: token's user must be an org member; for orgs with SAML SSO,
#   go to github.com/settings/tokens and click "Configure SSO" / "Authorize" for the org
# - Fine-grained PAT: needs "Contents" read/write and "Metadata" read for target repos
#
# GITHUB_OWNER (optional, default: wiki-as-git):
# - Set to your GitHub username to push to your account instead of the org
GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...
# GITHUB_OWNER=your-username
